Subject: Reflective KV Cache
Description: Fork-local architecture note for making KV cache address typed semantic and transformer-structural references, not only raw token-derived key/value tensors.

& [ReflectiveKVCache] is the proposed extension of Ollama's cache model
  + [source_specification] is C:\Project\ReasoningFramework\platform\source_documents\2026-05-31_ollama_reflective_kv_cache\Canonical_Reflective_KV_Cache_Specification.sop
  + [implementation_package] is kvcache
  + [first_slice] is typed reference records and validation only

  + [reference_layer] is one of surface, subtext, contract, structural, or reflective
    + [surface] is literal token-span context
    + [subtext] is typed interpretive state such as tone, implication, ambiguity, or authority tension
    + [contract] is durable rule or obligation identity such as an SOP contract
    + [structural] is subject, file, dependency, provenance, or runtime structure identity
    + [reflective] is transformer-internal parameter or activation address identity

  + [parameter_address] is a stable runtime address into a transformer tensor
    + [layer] is the transformer layer index
    + [module] is the owning runtime module or projection name
    + [tensor] is the tensor name
    + [offset] is the flattened tensor start index
    + [size] is the number of addressed scalar values

  + [activation_address] is a stable runtime address into layer/head/channel activation state
    + [layer] is the transformer layer index
    + [head] is the attention head index
    + [begin] is the first addressed channel
    + [end] is the exclusive addressed channel bound

  + [model_fingerprint] is the model-local identity needed before reflective addresses can be compared
    + [architecture] is the architecture family declared by model metadata
    + [family] is the model family or variant when available
    + [tokenizer] is the tokenizer identity when available
    + [digest] is a model or artifact digest when available

  + [address_space] is the model-scoped namespace for reflective addresses
    + [name] is the runtime or adapter namespace, such as llama.cpp
    + [version] is the address encoding version
    + [model_fingerprint] is the model-local identity carried by the namespace

  + [cache_cell_address] is a stable address into cache storage metadata
    + [cache] is the cache implementation name
    + [layer] is the active layer
    + [sequence] is the sequence id
    + [position] is the token position
    + [cell] is the cache cell index

  + [source_address] is a rehydration handle for exact source text outside active KV state
    + [path] is a source file path
    + [digest] is a content or artifact digest
    + [section] is an optional source-local section anchor
    + [line_range] is an optional exact line range
    + [byte_range] is an optional exact byte range

  + [reference_store] is a non-invasive index of validated references by stable key
  + [reference_resolver] is the interface that maps a reference and operation into an inspectable result
    + [operation] is inspect, retrieve, pin, evict, rehydrate, gate, or annotate
  + [reference_producer] is a non-invasive annotation producer that emits references from source documents
    + [source_document] is path, digest, optional section, and exact source text
    + [reference_annotation] is a reference plus current or stale annotation status
    + [sop_reference_producer] emits surface references for non-empty source lines
    + [sop_reference_producer] emits structural references for subject, field, enum, source, and composition declarations
    + [sop_reference_producer] emits contract references for directive and constraint lines
    + [sop_reference_producer] emits subtext references for question and assumption lines

  = must: keep current inference behavior unchanged in the first slice
  = must: validate references before any future runtime resolver consumes them
  = must: produce stable keys so typed references can later be joined, indexed, or compared
  = must: include address_space for reflective parameter, activation, and cache-cell references
  = must: escape reserved stable-key delimiters inside user or source supplied values
  = must: preserve source provenance on generated annotations
  = must: let annotations be marked stale without mutating their original reference keys
  = must: preserve exact source text outside this cache layer when exact recall matters
  - never: claim KV-cache reduction or accuracy preservation until benchmarked
